    "result_text": "The build is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite, and it passes along with the full `mvn test` run.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, emitted alongside the existing audit line in the owner-create flow.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **An immutable event record** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String customerCode, Integer membershipLevel, String event)`, a Java `record` so it's structurally immutable.\n\n2. **A monotonic sequence** \u2014 `AtomicLong AUDIT_SEQ`, incremented once per create, so `seq` strictly increases across all creates (thread-safe, static across the controller).\n\n3. **JSON serialization** \u2014 a static Jackson `ObjectMapper` (`JsonMapper`, matching the `tools.jackson` usage already in the codebase) serializes the event; the emitted line is a JSON object logged via the same `AUDIT` logger, e.g.:\n   ```\n   {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n   ```\n\n4. **A forward-looking identifier seam** \u2014 the event's identifier value comes from a new `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. This is the single point the spec's evolution note calls for: when the customerCode is later unified into a `memberId`, changing only that one method makes every emitted event carry the `memberId` instead, with no other change to the event's shape.\n\nThe `membershipLevel` is sourced from `ownerMapper.membershipLevel(owner)`, so it already reflects any household cap applied at creation \u2014 consistent with the existing audit line.",
